  "articleBody": "Nobody wants to spend time on a drywall repair only to have it look worse than before! There are some super common mistakes that can really trip you up. First off, a lot of people use the wrong texture method or apply texture only to the damaged spot instead of feathering it out. That's a surefire way to make the repair obvious. Another big one is skipping primer – it's crucial for getting an even paint finish. And here's a biggie: painting before the texture is fully dry. Joint compound needs a lot of time to dry completely, often 12-24 hours or even more depending on how thick it is and your home's humidity. Rushing this step can lead to cracks or an uneven look. Lastly, mixing compound too thick or too thin can make application a nightmare and the final result pretty sad. If you’re dealing with a large area, a complex texture, or if you’ve tried DIY repairs before with less-than-stellar results, it might be time to bring in the experts. HH Remodeling LLC can handle those tricky repairs and ensure a smooth, professional finish. You can reach Abraham and the team at 303-505-0866.",
